questions some that actually have clear  answers there's not so much  since helen died in the original  candyman movie it's completely sensible  that her character might be brought back  in flashback scenes in the new version  which is technically a sequel so where  is she instead of using footage from the  original film or digitally de-aging  virginia madsen to retell helen's story  nia de costa and jordan peel creatively  bring her back in different forms  instead of conventional flashback scenes  helen's tale is first told through  shadow puppetry which decosta said at a  press event for candyman presented her a  creative option not to rely on flashback  scenes for the most part the director  said she wanted this movie to stand on  its own and not to rely too explicitly  on the original movie from there she  said it just sort of became really less  about flashbacks and more about how we  depict people telling these stories how  would depict these legends and also we'd  pick these moments of violence  throughout history madsen does  eventually appear in the film very  briefly when anthony sees an old image  of her in a newspaper report detailing  how she was implicated in murders in the  cabrini green neighborhood madsen's  voice is also heard in tapes that  anthony gains access to in a library in  a curious casting move there's a tough  highbrow art critic assessing anthony's  exhibit finley stevens who resembles a  young madsen decosta said at the  candyman press event that spence's  resemblance to the original film star  was by mere happenstance and not design  surrender to me now  candyman wouldn't be the same without  tony todd's involvement in the film in  some capacity and yes he does turn up in  the film in a very meaningful cameo  appearance but what role does he play  since candyman 2021 is a creation  combining old and new ideas peel and  acosta went a different direction when  it came to working in a major theme in  the film that was clearly inspired by  the current climate and social justice  movements instead of todd's daniel  robitaille being featured throughout the  film he is referenced to by the adult  bobby as one of several to have suffered  the same sort of racial injustice that  befell sherman fields the iteration of  the candyman featured most prominently  in this new version that's not to say  however that fields is the only version  of candyman who appears in the new  iteration of the tale  anthony develops burn-like lesions on  his right hand after the ghost of  candyman materializes and kills his  first two victims news outlets naturally  detail the horrific incident and a  reporter on the scene divulges to her  audience a title of the exhibit say my  name the reporter also refers to the  painter as rising star anthony mccoy  much to the surprise of the artist who  is watching coverage on television at  that point in the film it appears  anthony is consumed by the newfound fame  the tragedy has brought him even though  the murders are responsible for it after  the reports he says almost giddily say  my name as a way to embrace his  notoriety so why does anthony obsess  over his candyman exhibit longing for  more fame is morbid curiosity in the  candyman legend deepens and he begins to  do more research and while anthony  suffers horrific hallucinations as a  result his obsession continues to  inspire more images as he parlays his  initial creation into a larger exhibit i  feel really connected to this story  one anthony doesn't realize is that he  has fallen under the spell of the  candyman curse and is somehow tied to a  tragic event involving the spirit  decades prior which is fully revealed  later in the film at that point though  anthony has entered the point of no  return his fate is sealed  no there isn't anything wrong with the  projection so what's with the reversed  logos the backwards logos for universal  pictures mgm braun and monkey paw  productions at the beginning of the film  were done on purpose presumably in an  homage to candyman lore after all the  spirit of a candyman doesn't materialize  in physical form only in a reflection in  the mirror the studio and peel are  clearly making a visual reference to the  legend by showing their logos backwards  much like a reflection in a mirror not  surprisingly mirrors appear everywhere  in candyman they are at anthony's  exhibit which is the location where  candyman kills his first two victims and  an elevator anthony takes in the  libraries made up entirely of mirrors  brianna attempts fade by standing in  front of a mirror yet doesn't give in to  her impulses but a group of high school  girls laugh off the legend and say  candyman's name five times and pay  dearly for it  as fans well know by now saying  candyman's name five times in a mirror  is what's needed to summon the violent  spirit however in the age of the social  justice movement in the u.s over the  past few years following the high  profile deaths of black people across  the country during altercations with  police certain phrases now have greater  meaning so what's the significance of  say my name calling on people to say the  names of the dead has become a prominent  part to the public conversation in  recent years and throughout the making  of the film the thing that i always came  back to is the truth of the pain that  was at the center of the story of  candyman in this way say my name serves  a dual purpose it's the title of  anthony's exhibit daring patrons of his  work to say candyman five times to find  out if the legend is indeed real and an  artful play on the real life phrases  used to call attention to and  memorialize the dead  with a bloody third act that leads to  the transformation of a key character  into the new candyman peel and acosta  have left the door wide open for more  candyman films but will we get them  naturally the production of a sequel for  any film is dependent on the box office  success of its predecessor so the new  candyman will have to be a big enough  hit with moviegoers at the box office  and on home video to justify universal  and mgm's investment in a sequel the  good news for peel and acosta is that  candy man was made for around 25 million  dollars a relatively small amount by  modern standards even with the covet 19  pandemic still wreaking havoc on box  office returns the new candyman  shouldn't have much trouble making its  money back as the 1992 version of  candyman demonstrated there is more room  for additional tales about the character  should peel and acosta wish to move in  that direction the original film spawned  two sequels candyman farewell to the  flesh in 1995 and candyman day of the  dead in 1999 will this new imagining  return for further stories we'll just  have to say the name and see  [Music]  don't say that  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite horror movies are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]
 

